    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "The Sartorius PMA is a family of self-indicating, single-interval, non-automatic weighing instruments designed to be used in paint mixing applications. The family comprises the PMA-EV (Class II) and the PMA-HD (Class III) types, each comprising several models. The instrument shall not be used for direct sales to the public. Construction: plastic construction, stainless steel load receptor, plastic display head, 3 feet (2 adjustable), level indicator, LCD segment display with fixed position touch keys (EVO1, LAB1, SPO1), LCD graphic display with touch function (VIS1), EX-link converter for voltage supply and data transfer (X and Y models except EVO1Y). Devices: initial zero setting device (max 20% of Max), zero tracking device (max 4% of Max), zero indicator (PMA-HD only), combined zero-setting and tare-balancing device, preset tare device (only via a PC), approximate displaying device (PMA-EV only), weight accumulation, weight calculating. A PC with compatible paint mixing software can be connected via the interfaces provided; all devices can be initiated via a PC, preset tare can only be introduced via a PC. Interfaces: USB either directly (S models and EVO1Y) or via Ex-link converter (EVO1X and LAB1X); Ethernet via Ex-link converter (VIS1X and VIS1Y models). Power supply: 5 V DC provided by USB; for X and Y models except EVO1Y, power is delivered from USB to the Ex-link converter and then to the instrument via RJ-45. Software: permitted versions are weighing instrument software BAC (ID 05496, or 1578 for VIS models, version 00-56-02.xx) and software application APC (only VIS models, ID 6587, version 01-72-03.xx), where xx reflects legally non-relevant changes. Sealing: access to the electronics and load cell is prevented by two tamper-evident labels on the underside of the instrument; access to the Menu access switch is prevented by a tamper-evident label covering the switch."
  },
